--- REPO NOTE (not part of the cluster README below) ---

Synced from MareNostrum 5, /gpfs/scratch/uv36/adrian/deepmd-training/RESULTS, on
10/10/2026. This is pure post-processing: no MD and no DFT is run here.

Scope of what was committed: everything, including all 814 per-grid-point speciation
diagrams (about 137 MB). They are genuinely distinct files, one pair per concentration
grid point, not duplicates -- the complete 20x20 grid is here rather than a sample. The
scientific summary of the whole grid is in 'speciation/speciation_grid_analysis.txt' if
you want the conclusions without opening 814 figures.

One artefact of the deduplication used across this sync: the eight
'concentrations_vs_pH_<Mg>_<PP>.dat' files now sit at this top level rather than inside
their grid-point folders. Each of them was byte-identical in two places on the cluster --
once under 'speciation/<MMMM_PPPP>/' where it was produced and once under
'energies/<MMMM_PPPP>/' where it was copied as input -- so it is committed once at the
directory covering both. On the cluster they exist in both places.

Read 'speciation/README' first, then 'energies/README'. The second one records the trap
that matters most here: the 'energies/' subfolders belong to two incompatible generations
of the same calculation and the folder names do not say which.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Cluster README follows:
----------------------------------------------------------------------

=====================================
FOLDER: RESULTS
SYSTEM: MareNostrum 5 — glogin2
CREATED: 06/08/2026
UPDATED: 01/10/2026
PURPOSE: Thermodynamic/kinetic modelling of the Mg(II)-pyrophosphate system as a
         function of pH. Pure post-processing: no MD and no DFT is run here.
=====================================

06/08/2026

o Analysis outputs derived from the project's speciation and thermodynamic
  modelling, separate from the MD/DFT pipelines elsewhere in this tree.

01/10/2026

o Expanded this file to cover both subfolders, since 'energies/' was previously
  undocumented. The two form a pipeline and should be read in order.

o 'speciation/' solves the equilibrium speciation of the eleven-species
  Mg(II)/pyrophosphate system over pH, on a 20x20 grid of total Mg and total PP
  concentrations, 400 runs. It answers which species are present at which pH.
  See 'speciation/README', which is detailed and includes the grid-wide analysis.

o 'energies/' takes a speciation curve from the above, combines it with a
  hand-entered table of per-species activation barriers, and returns a
  Boltzmann-weighted effective barrier and Eyring rate constant versus pH, with
  and without magnesium, including a comparison against Wolfenden's experimental
  data. See 'energies/README'. That README also records the one thing that will
  mislead a reader otherwise: the subfolders there belong to two incompatible
  generations of the calculation, and the top-level script is not the one that
  produced the newer ones.

o 'bulk.sh' is the driver that built the speciation grid. It loops total Mg and
  total PP from 5 to 100 mM in 5 mM steps, creates each 'MMMM_PPPP' folder, uses
  'sed' to substitute the two concentrations into a frozen copy of
  'speciation/speciation.py', and runs it there. Note it only generates the
  speciation side; the 'energies/' runs were launched by hand.
